{
  "conclusion": {
    "headline": "CURRENT DATA = results/timed_bench.csv (run_version ritzfix_v2, 456 runs: fixed-n 204 + timed 252, 3 seeds). The 2D Ritz objective was corrected to a variational QR-projection eigh; ALL PRIOR B PERFORMANCE NUMBERS (complete_ci 576, earlier timed curves, walltime ratios) are INVALID_RITZ_OBJECTIVE and retracted. Per-cell median dE (3 seeds) in experiments.fixed_walltime_bench: no single method wins across all systems. At fixed n, orbital-optimized Slater is best on Hubbard (L6 U1 @n=12 med 4.6e-3 vs CIPSI 2.85, replica 2.85); replica convex-J tracks CIPSI almost exactly on Hubbard but is slightly better on H2 mid-n. At fixed walltime 1.5s L6 U1 orbopt med 2.9e-3 beats CIPSI 0.34, but L6 U8 CIPSI 0.015 beats orbopt 0.23. Throughput != energy; no universal winner and no advertised speedup.",
